 "summary": "Budjala territory (Sud-Ubangi), between Gemena and the Ubangi/Mongala, lies far from the eastern and Mai-Ndombe conflict zones and no Congolese or foreign armed group is known to hold territory there. Budjala town, the territory seat, is administered by the territorial authorities with Congolese National Police (PNC) commissariats; secteur centres (Bangabola, Bulu, Mbaya, Ndage) and villages fall under PNC posts, territorial administration and customary chiefs. Known insecurity consists of ordinary crime, abuses by state agents and land/customary disputes, which do not amount to territorial control by another actor. Web search was unavailable in this run (search budget exhausted, news sites blocked), so the assessment rests on default state presence and general knowledge, with low confidence for rural villages.",
